{title: Lord, Speak to Me}
{artist: Frances R. Havergal / Robert Schumann}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: G}
{tempo: 105}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (United Methodist Hymnal (Nashville, Tennessee: United Methodist Publishing House, 1989), # 463)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Lord, [G]speak to [Em]me [Am]that [D7]I may [G]speak
[G]In [C]living [G]echoes [D]of [A7]Thy [D7]tone;
[D7]As [G]Thou [B]has [E]sought, [Am]so [D7]let me [G]seek
[G]Thine [C]erring [G]children [D7]lost and [G]lone.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
[D]O [G]use me, [Em]Lord, [Am]use [D7]even [G]me,
[G]Just [C]as Thou [G]wilt, and [D]when, [A7]and [D7]where,
[D7]Un[G]til [B]Thy [E]bless[Am]èd [D7]face I [G]see,
[G]Thy [C]rest, Thy [G]joy, Thy [D7]glory [G]share.
{end_of_verse}
